# 🏗️ SQL Data Warehouse & Analytics Project

## 📖 Project Overview

This project demonstrates the end-to-end construction of a scalable **Data Warehouse** using **Microsoft SQL Server**.

It follows the **Medallion Architecture** (Bronze → Silver → Gold) to efficiently ingest, clean, transform, and model raw data from disparate sources (CRM & ERP systems) into a structured analytics-ready format.

The final layer powers a comprehensive suite of SQL analytics, providing actionable business intelligence on sales performance, customer behavior, and product trends.


# **🏗️ Architecture & Data Pipeline**

The project is structured into three distinct layers to ensure data quality, reliability, and performance:

## **1. 🥉 Bronze Layer (Raw Staging)**

**Purpose:** Initial ingestion of raw data from source systems.

**Process:** CSV files from CRM (cust_info, prd_info, sales_details) and ERP (CUST_AZ12, LOC_A101, PX_CAT_G1V2) systems are bulk-loaded into SQL tables via stored procedures.

**Key Feature:** Acts as a historical archive, preserving source data in its original form for full auditability.


## **2. 🥈 Silver Layer (Cleansed & Enriched)**

**Purpose:** Data cleansing, standardization, and integration.

**Key Transformations:**

Deduplication of customer records.

Standardization of values (e.g., marital status, country names).

Data Validation (e.g., correcting invalid dates).

Text Cleaning and null handling.

ID Normalization for consistent joins.

**Outcome:** Creates a single, trusted source of truth by merging and refining data from both CRM and ERP systems.


## **3. 🥇 Gold Layer (Business-Ready Schema)**

**Purpose:** Model data into an optimized star schema for analytics.

**Structure:**

**Dimensions:** dim_customers, dim_products

**Facts:** fact_sales

**Process:** Applies final business logic and joins to create intuitive, query-friendly tables ready for reporting.



# **📊 Analytics & Business Insights**
The Gold layer enables deep analysis through a series of SQL queries designed to answer critical business questions:

**Performance Analysis:** Identified top 10 customers and top/bottom 5 products by revenue.

**Trend Analysis:** Calculated Year-Over-Year (YoY) sales growth and cumulative running totals.

**Geographic Analysis:** Broke down sales and customers by country.

**Product Analysis:** Revenue contribution by category and product cost segmentation.

**Customer Segmentation:** Classified customers into VIP, Regular, and New based on lifetime value and tenure.

# **🛠️ Technical Skills Demonstrated**
**Database:** Microsoft SQL Server

**Architecture:** Medallion Architecture

**ETL/ELT:** BULK INSERT, Stored Procedures, Data Truncation

**Data Modeling:** Star Schema, Dimension & Fact Tables

**Data Transformation:** Deduplication, Standardization, Validation, Type Casting

**Advanced SQL:**

Window Functions (ROW_NUMBER(), LAG(), DENSE_RANK())

CTEs, Subqueries

Conditional Logic (CASE statements)

Date Functions (DATEDIFF, DATETRUNC)

Joins & Aggregations (SUM, COUNT, AVG)
